# Vendored canonical artifacts (contracts/, content-schema/schemas/vendor/) are
# byte-exact copies verified by SHA-256 checksum against provenance.json. Any
# EOL normalization (e.g. core.autocrlf=true converting LF -> CRLF on
# checkout) silently changes their bytes without a semantic diff, breaking
# checksum verification. Mark them binary so Git never rewrites their bytes,
# regardless of the developer's global core.autocrlf setting.
packages/contracts/vendor/** -text
packages/content-schema/schemas/vendor/** -text
